# Canonical line endings for a byte-exact repository.
#
# Why this file exists: this repository relies on SHA-256 byte-exact artifacts —
#   * evals/external-v2/frozen/** + freeze-manifest.json (External Eval v2 evidence), and
#   * dsh/skill/effective-thinking.md (must equal the canonical SKILL.md body byte-for-byte).
# Git's default `core.autocrlf` behaviour would rewrite LF to CRLF on a Windows checkout, which
# changes those bytes and makes `verify-freeze` / `dsh:check` fail on an unmodified tree.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` normalizes text files to LF in the working tree on every platform, so the
# bytes are identical regardless of the OS doing the checkout. This does NOT rewrite history: it
# only affects how files are checked out from now on.
#
# Deliberately NOT using `* -text`: that would disable normalization entirely and leave files at
# the mercy of each machine's autocrlf setting.

* text=auto eol=lf

# ---- Binary: never touch these bytes ----
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
*.tgz  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary

# ---- Explicitly canonical-LF text (byte-exact contracts) ----
# Frozen evidence: hashed by freeze-manifest.json; must never be rewritten by git.
evals/external-v2/frozen/**    text eol=lf
evals/external-v2/**           text eol=lf
# Canonical skill + its packaged, byte-compared DSH twin.
SKILL.md                       text eol=lf
dsh/skill/effective-thinking.md text eol=lf
dsh/cordis.patch.yml           text eol=lf
LICENSE                        text eol=lf

# ---- Windows-only scripts (if any are ever added) keep CRLF for the shell that reads them ----
*.bat  text eol=crlf
*.cmd  text eol=crlf
*.ps1  text eol=crlf
